WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.040
Just being at your side,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:16.160
Gentles my hearts to the point of disbelief

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:25.570
I thought I heard the sound of your footsteps behind me,

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:35.720
I turned my head repeatedly, wishing you would appear...

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.740
...and then there you were

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:50.990
The beginning of a new love

00:00:51.310 --> 00:01:05.870
Is unknowingly, the beginning of our invisible love story

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:15.360
Hence, I shall never leave your side

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.540
I pledge to love you and only you

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.720
You're eloping? At a time like this?

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.730
Oh well, you're young.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.190
Why not do it while you can?

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:49.330
<i>Just Chise and me, five days</i> <i>after we fled our town.</i>

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.260
<i>We closed our eyes...</i>

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.450
<i>to the world, the people</i> <i>and everything in it.</i>

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.510
<i>We vowed to see only the happiness...</i>

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.370
<i>the precious and irreplaceable things...</i>

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.960
TOMATOES<b>
</b>FOR THE<b>
</b>THANKS<b></b>

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>the precious and irreplaceable things...</i>

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.220
<i>that lay in front of us.</i>

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.620
Shuji, look!

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:15.680
Quickly!

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.520
The sea! A harbor!

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:26.470
<i>We'd made it to a town like our own,</i>

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.030
<i>looking out at the sea.</i>

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.530
This place is fine. Here I can...

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:41.590
"A Time for Us"
Episode 11

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.760
Hey rookie!

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:48.340
Coming!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.530
Hey, Ferret!

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:55.730
"Ferret"?

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.790
Yeah, you! Why d'you have such a sorry lunch?

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.470
You're in a good mood, Masa.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.670
I just had ramen over at "Tetsuryu."

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.240
How's the new girl?

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.060
Cute as a button! Working so hard...

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.250
She'll be a big help to "the General."

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.180
Since his wife died, he's been working alone.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.010
Welcome!

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:22.360
Well, she is pretty clumsy.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.090
But that's cute too!

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.790
Think so?

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.930
<i>For the first time, it was just us.</i>

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.700
<i>Chise and I were living</i> <i>with all our hearts...</i>

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:44.050
<i>as if this gentle,</i> <i>heartrending happiness...</i>

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.380
<i>would never end.</i>

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:08.370
Chise!

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.040
Shuji!

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.240
Sorry I'm late!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:13.680
You must be tired.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.220
Aren't you cold?

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:16.780
Cold?

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.000
Oh, yeah! It's freezing!

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:23.010
Hey, look!

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.650
This fish soup's great!

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.580
We had it at dinner, but I wanted you to try it.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.620
"The General" gave me a cabbage...

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:35.360
for working so hard.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.260
Then, tonight we'll have cabbage and soup!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.200
Yeah!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:14.870
Shuji...

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.100
We're happy, aren't we?

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.670
Shuji...

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:25.340
We are, right?

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.020
Shuji...

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.310
<i>What would our life be like,</i> <i>in this town?</i>

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.260
<i>I couldn't answer that.</i>

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.210
<i>Just as I had no way of knowing...</i>

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.800
<i>why Chise had cried that night.</i>

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.420
Laundry day, laundry day...

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.360
here we go...

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:19.390
Why go there after work if Chise's not there?

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:21.370
That's true.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:22.420
Shuji!

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:24.890
You don't have an umbrella!

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.130
Let's go!

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.270
OK!

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.070
See you.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:29.940
- Huh? - Huh?

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.450
What?! Ferret and Chise?!

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:48.470
You're up early.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.360
Yeah, good morning, Shuji.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:51.830
'Morning.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.260
Going to work?

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:55.900
Yeah.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.240
What?

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:01.410
No, don't go.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:02.960
I'm lonely.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.460
Don't say that. It's my job.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.760
Uh, I forgot my umbrella.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:38.510
<i>That day, for the first time,</i> <i>we both skipped work.</i>

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.080
<i>We fooled around a bit...</i>

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.620
<i>cuddling and touching each other...</i>

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:49.320
<i>seeking each other's body</i> <i>with kiss after kiss.</i>

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.060
<i>With my body's heat and kisses,</i>

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:57.330
<i>Chise's cold skin grew warm and moist.</i>

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.070
<i>That, I thought,</i>

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.540
<i>was happiness of a sort.</i>

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.330
Chise, what time is it?

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.190
It's past noon, Shuji.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.260
Already?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:00.720
Chise...

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:01.560
Huh?

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.200
Oh, no!

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.760
I guess from all the excitement.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.470
Are you alright?

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:12.140
It's OK, I feel fine!

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.210
Shuji, thank you.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:23.180
I know I'm going to be happy for the rest of my life.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.720
Home-cooked lunch?

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.260
Nice, eh?

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:35.530
Come on, guys!

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:36.730
Hey, Masa...

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.430
Hey, Shuji!

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.740
What's that for, Masa?

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.810
Chise's not at work today!

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:43.900
What?

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.710
You've gotta tell me these things!

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.220
Chise...

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:07.390
Shuji...

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:08.930
Chise.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.370
I'm sorry, Shuji.

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:47.480
<i>These are just vitamins.</i> <i>A girl's gotta take care of herself...</i>

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:55.180
<i>She's made of the same elements</i> <i>that make up any human being.</i>

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.610
<i>No one can save her</i> <i>from her fate.</i>

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.550
Fifty! A new record!

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.980
Congrats, Chise!

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.060
Welco...

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:18.300
There's no point repairing the nets anymore, Ferret.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.400
There're no more fish out there.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:27.640
It's all over. We were lucky to have lasted this long.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.570
Your miso ramen.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.390
Uh, thanks.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.250
- There you go. <i>- I told you to stay away.</i>

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:35.740
- So sorry. <i> -Can you hear me?</i>

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:38.290
- Did I splash you? <i>- It's encrypted.</i>

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:42.690
<i>Only you can receive this.</i>

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.560
What would you like to order?

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:50.500
<i>Why are you here?</i> <i>I'll kill you, too.</i>

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.470
It's my job. It can't be helped.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:12:00.740
<i>You never learn.</i> <i>Your work is meaningless now.</i>

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:02.460
And your medicine?

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:07.980
<i>It ran out, but I'm still alive.</i> <i>Is that because I'm in love?</i>

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.810
But... you won't last long.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:17.490
<i>Shuji and I haven't had</i> <i>much time together,</i>

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:21.390
<i>but it's been good.</i> <i>My heart is always pounding.</i>

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.430
<i>I'm so small,</i>

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:25.600
<i>if I still had a heart,</i>

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:32.370
<i>I'm sure it would burst with</i> <i>how much love I feel.</i>

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.040
Enjoy.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:36.870
Your ramen's getting cold.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.820
<i>I even put something special</i> <i>in it for you,</i>

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:43.210
<i>that thing you developed</i> <i>with such a high...</i>

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:45.080
<i>rate of kill.</i>

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:49.720
<i>I'm sorry, I didn't mean that.</i>

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:51.090
<i>I'm kidding.</i>

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:02.840
No. Stop it. Please don't kill anymore.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:06.900
Be good, OK?

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.940
Please, you too, Mr. Kawahara...

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:14.140
Stay away!

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:17.380
Leave us alone!

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:24.620
Uh...

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.150
I'm working now.

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:28.930
Have you had your fun?

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:34.900
She's almost out of time. The only thing that can save her...

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.590
is battle.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:41.260
I'm not saying this because it's my job.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:45.970
I want to save her. That's all!

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:51.950
She needs us as much as we need her!

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:55.750
Is this Chise's life?

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.680
There's still some left?

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.480
Well, that won't be enough.

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.660
Answer me! Is this Chise's life?

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.460
What happens when these run out?

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:12.670
Only battle can save her.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.310
It's not her fault.

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:19.140
Or yours, or ours.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:21.190
It can't be helped.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:25.390
I don't know what will happen if she's left alone.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:26.790
She's dangerous!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.090
Enough.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.660
Go back to your family.

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:40.530
Chise's my wife. I won't let her kill anymore.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.200
When the time comes...

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.140
I'll kill her myself.

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:03.620
Will it work? Can you fix it, Shuji?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:08.390
I hope so. I'm gonna try.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.160
Chise, let's find a new place.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:15.370
Huh?

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:19.100
Sorry, but I'm bored of this place.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.180
The job, the town, everything.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.180
Yeah. I'm bored too.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:33.990
Chise, if I can get this bike running,

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.690
let's go on a picnic!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:37.420
Huh?

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:40.330
I'll do my best.

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:43.300
Like, a date?

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.570
First one since the aquarium.

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:47.170
Yeah!

00:15:48.270 --> 00:15:49.000
It'll be fun.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:49.960
Let's go!

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:58.840
Oh, yeah.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.750
I forgot I have something for you, Chise.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:04.220
Hold out your hand.

00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:05.550
What is it?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.300
A while ago, that old geezer gave me them.

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.570
How long...will they last?

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:24.210
Just a bit.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.710
Right then! I'll get this bike running!

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:33.410
Tomorrow, I'll ask Masa to help me.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:41.310
Good luck.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:46.250
A picnic... that'll be fun.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:47.930
Yeah.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:56.600
Get this bike going?

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:58.240
Please!

00:16:58.310 --> 00:17:00.280
No way.

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:02.210
Alright, Ferret.

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:06.950
You give me the lunch Chise makes for three days.

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:10.820
I'll have it running.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:13.790
Thank you, Masa!

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.380
Hey! Big news!

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.330
Hey, music...

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:33.170
Someone's broadcasting.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:37.940
What's this song? It sounds familiar.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.120
I'm all choked up!

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:43.510
They say it's been playing continuously for a week.

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:47.140
It's a nice song, anyway.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:53.060
But maybe Chise'd prefer something more current...

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:54.150
<i>But first...</i>

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:58.360
<i>what's a "song"?</i>

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:04.870
<i>I'm scared!</i>

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:07.040
<i>Scared!</i>

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:11.310
<i>Is this it? I'm scared!</i>

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:14.250
<i>Am I still human?</i>

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:16.780
<i>Am I dying?</i>

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.680
<i>No, a weapon?</i>

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:35.090
<i>What's this...?</i>

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:38.990
<i>What...</i>

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.030
<i>Oh, I remember!</i>

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:46.660
<i>That's the song Shuji hums when</i> <i>he's in a good mood.</i>

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:48.330
<i>I remember.</i>

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.040
<i>That's a "song."</i>

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:57.100
<i>A love song.</i>

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:02.680
Shuji, I'm a bit tired. I'll go lie down upstairs.

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:12.790
See? Told you I could fix it.

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:18.230
Chise makes a great lunch!

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:19.810
Thanks so much!

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:20.770
Yup!

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.960
I saw something like that... in the movies.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.120
Masa...

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:43.570
Nice bike. Chise'll love it...

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:54.540
Chise!

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.240
- You came for me! <i>- Don't look.</i>

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:02.770
- What can I do?! <i>- I can end the pain.</i>

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:03.780
Help me!

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:05.680
Where's everyone?

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:06.910
<i>Shall I kill him?</i>

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.150
Chise, Chise...

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:14.420
<i>- Don't touch me.</i> - No, Shuji!

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:16.960
<i>- I'll kill you.</i> - Don't do it!

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:18.080
<i>Shall I?</i>

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:22.660
<i>I'd let her...</i>

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:24.560
<i>kill me.</i>

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.060
<i>The pain...</i>

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:29.160
<i>I've never felt this before.</i>

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:31.440
<i>It can't be helped.</i>

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.470
<i>I'm embracing a weapon, after all.</i>

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:40.190
What can I do, Shuji?! They're all dying!

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:43.610
The "General's" dead!

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:45.520
Chise! Chise!

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:49.860
Why is this happening to me?!

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:53.160
Nooo! I'm breaking down!

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:58.200
<i>Was this what Chise had</i> <i>been going through...</i>

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:00.860
<i>day after day after day?</i>

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:06.100
<i>Was this the stabbing pain</i> <i>she endured every day...</i>

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:08.170
<i>while still managing...</i>

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:13.200
<i>to breathe, to live?</i>

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.650
This is my punishment, Shuji.

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:24.420
For all the joy I've stolen, the crimes I've committed...

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.960
while still staying alive like a regular person.

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:32.060
No, better than them, because I could have...

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:37.440
two weeks of happiness with you.

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:39.870
I'm sorry.

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:41.970
Sorry, to everyone.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:48.310
As strong as I am, in the end, I could do nothing.

00:21:50.650 --> 00:21:52.810
They're here!

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:53.850
I have to go!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:55.290
No, Chise!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:56.950
Chise! Chise!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:58.720
No more.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:00.670
That's enough.

00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:04.160
It's OK, Chise.

00:22:05.270 --> 00:22:08.780
Chise, I'll... kill you, alright?!

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:12.530
I'll kill you!

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:16.710
Shuji...

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:43.420
A rift opened up upon my heart

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:49.990
And I went through the night sleepless, sighing constantly

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:59.340
Before I realize, it's turned to morning

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:08.660
I want to hear your voice

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:13.250
I want to feel your warmth

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:19.460
Thoughts of you well up within me

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:25.310
And my tears begin to overflow

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:36.570
Goodbye my beloved, I am still unable to forget about you

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:46.740
Having all of this end with just a single word of goodbye

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:51.570
Fills me with sorrow

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:04.380
Chise, are you going to die on me? Just like Akemi?

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:05.950
What should I do?!

00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:08.780
Oh, Chise, I can hear your voice...

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:10.280
It's a song.

00:24:10.490 --> 00:24:14.970
SAIKANO, Episode 12: "Love Song"
